[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/00-redux-header.png?v=ae09fac[/img]

[b][color=#B89CFF]Less mod chaos. More control.[/color][/b]

[url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux][b]GitHub & Documentation[/b][/url] • [url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/releases][b]Releases & Changelog[/b][/url] • [url=https://discord.gg/rJJF89vqFZ][b]Discord[/b][/url]
[/center]

[b]Baldur's Gate 3 Mod Manager Redux[/b] is a Windows community fork of [url=https://github.com/LaughingLeader/BG3ModManager][b]LaughingLeader's BG3 Mod Manager[/b][/url], built to make your mod setup easier to organize, understand, and maintain.

Keep the familiar Active, Inactive, and Override panes, profiles, and drag-and-drop load orders. Add a redesigned interface, collapsible sections, built-in diagnostics, download and save managers, custom themes, and tools for backing up and restoring your setup.

[quote]
[color=#F0B44D][b]Public alpha — actively developed, with bugs still expected.[/b][/color]
Redux is developed and maintained primarily by me. Testing cannot cover every mod list or Windows setup, so keep independent backups of important mods, profiles, and saves. Reports and feedback help shape the next build.
[/quote]


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/02-main-features.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[list]
[*][b]Make a large library manageable.[/b] Use categories, nested collapsible sections, filters, and saved orders to find what you need.[/*]
[*][b]See what will change.[/b] Review installs, game syncs, and optional load-order suggestions before applying them.[/*]
[*][b]Keep a way back.[/b] Use Undo/Redo, order history, restore points, and named snapshots for different kinds of recovery.[/*]
[*][b]Bring more of your setup together.[/b] Manage downloads, Nexus Collections, saves, and supported native plugins from Redux.[/*]
[*][b]Make the interface yours.[/b] Choose themes, fonts, text sizes, shortcuts, icons, and motion settings.[/*]
[/list]


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/10-installation.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[b]Requirements:[/b] Windows 10 or 11 (x64), Baldur's Gate 3, and the [url=https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/8.0][b].NET 8 Desktop Runtime[/b][/url]. Linux, macOS, Wine, and Proton are not supported platforms.

[list=1]
[*]Install the [b].NET 8 Desktop Runtime[/b].[/*]
[*]Download the [b]Portable ZIP[/b] from this Nexus page or [url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/releases][b]GitHub Releases[/b][/url]. Both receive the same approved archive.[/*]
[*]Extract the [b]entire ZIP[/b] into a dedicated writable folder, such as [b]C:\Modding\Redux[/b].[/*]
[*]Run [b]Redux.exe[/b], review the detected game and profile paths, and follow Welcome Setup.[/*]
[/list]

Do not run Redux inside the ZIP, the BG3 installation directory, or a protected Windows system folder.

[b]Already using BG3 Mod Manager?[/b] Redux can use the same BG3 Mods folder and profiles. Give Redux its own application folder, keep backups, and check the selected profile and order before syncing. Avoid running file operations in both managers at the same time.

[b]Updating Redux:[/b] use the built-in updater, or close Redux, back up its folder, and extract the complete newer archive over it. [b]Update & Back Up[/b] offers a pre-update ZIP; ordinary [b]Update & Restart[/b] does not create that backup. Preserve your Data, orders, downloads, retained archives, logs, caches, and backups during a routine update.

[url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/blob/main/docs/INSTALLATION.md][b]Full installation, update, migration & removal guide[/b][/url]


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/04-saving-and-syncing.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[heading][color=#B89CFF]From installed mod to game load order[/color][/heading]

[list=1]
[*][b]Install.[/b] Add a supported local package or install a completed download. New ordinary PAK mods enter [b]Inactive Mods[/b]; updates preserve an installed mod's active/inactive state and position where applicable.[/*]
[*][b]Activate and arrange.[/b] Move the mods you want into [b]Active Mods[/b], then arrange them according to the authors' instructions.[/*]
[*][b]Save.[/b] Store the working order in your selected Redux saved order.[/*]
[*][b]Sync Load Order to Game.[/b] Review what will activate, deactivate, or move, then confirm writing the result to BG3's [i]modsettings.lsx[/i].[/*]
[/list]

[b]Save keeps your Redux order. Sync changes the game's order.[/b] They are separate actions. Sync updates the game-backed [b]Current[/b] order without silently saving unfinished edits to a named order.

Named orders, comparisons, history, restore points, and Undo/Redo help you track changes. Redux also checks for external game-file changes before undoing a previous sync.

[heading][color=#B89CFF]Backups and snapshots[/color][/heading]

Open [b]Preferences > Backups[/b] or [b]Tools > Backups and snapshots[/b] to create a named snapshot of Redux's application files, settings, artwork, and saved orders. Enable [b]Include mods and mod lists[/b] to also capture BG3 PAKs, held Overrides, and profile load-order files.

Restoring verifies the archive and creates a return snapshot first, so you can restore that state again later. Restore replaces the included folders and can remove newer files from them; review the scope before proceeding.

[b]Snapshots exclude game saves and game-directory DLL/loose-texture mods.[/b] Pre-update ZIP backups also exclude saves. Keep independent copies of important files and use Save Game Manager for save exports.

[url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/blob/main/docs/BACKUPS.md][b]Snapshot contents, restore limits & recovery guide[/b][/url]


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/03-organization.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[b]Give every part of your library a place.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Categories:[/b] assign multiple labels per mod, with custom names, colors, icons, descriptions, and filters. Clear or restore automatic assignments while keeping manual choices.[/*]
[*][b]Separators and sub-separators:[/b] create named, collapsible sections with one level of nesting across Active, Inactive, and Override Mods. Move selected mods into nested or collapsed sections with Undo/Redo.[/*]
[*][b]Persistent organization:[/b] Inactive ordering and sections save automatically. Saved Active orders retain their own placement and collapsed state.[/*]
[*][b]Mod details:[/b] inspect descriptions, requirements, files, changelogs, source information, and diagnostics in the selected mod drawer. Add private notes, searchable local aliases, or custom preview artwork.[/*]
[*][b]Overrides per order:[/b] move Override PAKs between Inactive and Override Mods to record which are enabled for a saved order. Disabled PAKs stay in a Redux-managed folder. Orders without a recorded selection keep the previous all-Overrides behavior.[/*]
[/list]

Categories, section labels, icons, aliases, and notes never enter [i]modsettings.lsx[/i]. Dragging a collapsed Active section also moves its contained mods in the working order; enabling or disabling Overrides changes which PAK files are available to the game.

[b]Duplicate Override files?[/b] Use [b]Tools > Resolve Override Copies[/b] to compare copies, choose which to keep, and retain recovery backups.

[heading][color=#B89CFF]Share your setup with Redux Modlists[/color][/heading]

Export a [b].bg3redux Modlist[/b] with a saved order and selected categories, separators, icons, and public source links. Private notes are included only if you choose them. Imports and exports show a preview.

Modlists contain no PAKs, saves, profiles, or API keys, and importing one does not install missing mods.


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/05-downloads.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[b]Download, inspect, then decide what to install.[/b]

Download Manager handles supported local packages and optional Nexus [b]Mod Manager Download[/b] links. Downloads stay separate from installation, with progress, pause/resume/retry, restart recovery, and package verification.

Redux inspects packages and routes ordinary PAKs, saves, and reviewed native or Script Extender packages to the appropriate manager. [b]Install All[/b] gives you one grouped review of destinations and skipped items before installation.

Choose a managed Downloads folder in Preferences. Enable the optional [b]Package Archive Library[/b] to retain verified installation packages for reuse, within a configurable storage limit. Previous PAK versions have their own storage limit, separate from downloads.

[heading][color=#B89CFF]Nexus Collections[/color][/heading]

Choose [b]Import Nexus Collection[/b] and paste a BG3 collection page link to review its latest published revision.

[list]
[*]Compare collection files with Nexus-linked mods in Active and Inactive Mods.[/*]
[*]Skip exact installed files by default; filter Missing, Installed, Unverified, and Needs attention entries.[/*]
[*]Choose files to download and return to remembered selections in recent collections.[/*]
[*]Review and save a supported collection load order without activating mods or replacing your current order.[/*]
[/list]

Nexus integration requires API-key setup; manager downloads also use NXM link handling. Free accounts authorize individual files through [b]Mod Manager Download[/b]. Collection installer rules are not applied automatically, so follow the collection author's setup instructions.

[heading][color=#B89CFF]Check updates on your terms[/color][/heading]

Use [b]Mod Review > Check Mod Updates[/b], or right-click a linked Nexus mod and choose [b]Check Nexus File Update[/b]. Redux identifies verified replacement files and links to the affected mod pages; uncertain matches are not treated as confirmed updates.

[b]Skip this update[/b] hides specific offered replacements while allowing later updates to notify you. Use [b]Show skipped updates[/b] to bring those notifications back.


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/08-diagnostics-and-load-order-advisor.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[b]Understand the warnings before changing the order.[/b]

[b]Mod Diagnostics[/b] surfaces locally detectable dependencies, UUID problems, overrides, Mod Fixer behavior, Script Extender requirements, and package warnings. It is built in and read-only; diagnostics do not automatically repair, install, activate, or reorder mods.

The optional, experimental [b]Load Order Advisor[/b] uses package declarations, explicit offline rules, and labeled grouping suggestions to preview changes to Active Mods. Keep existing sections, replace them with suggested sections, or organize without sections. Applying a preview creates one unsaved, undoable edit.

[b]The Advisor cannot guarantee compatibility.[/b] Mod-author instructions still take priority.

The bundled offline database also helps identify mod sources. When the evidence is uncertain, a package stays [b]Local[/b]. You can help improve recognition by generating a contribution report containing sanitized identity information and fingerprints, without including PAKs, credentials, private notes, or filesystem paths.


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/06-save-game-manager.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[b]Find the campaign, inspect the save, review its mods.[/b]

Save Game Manager groups saves by campaign and shows available screenshots, dates, difficulty, location, party information, and mod counts.

[b]Review Mods[/b] compares recorded mod UUIDs with your installed library and highlights missing or inactive entries. You can activate installed inactive requirements with Undo support, then save and sync separately. This review does not verify required versions, dependency chains, or native mods.

Import save folders, loose [i].lsv[/i] files, or supported archives. Export saves or campaigns to ZIP within the export limits: [b]32 saves, 1 GB total, 256 MB per file[/b]. Normal deletion uses the Windows Recycle Bin.

[b]Close BG3 before changing saves and keep independent backups.[/b] Redux reads metadata; it does not repair save contents. Steam Cloud may restore files deleted locally.


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/07-game-directory-mods.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[b]Manage supported native mods alongside your PAK library.[/b]

Game-Directory Mod Manager handles a reviewed catalog of Script Extender, native, and root-level package layouts. It previews destinations, validates supported files, tracks ownership, and preserves originals where required. Unknown or modified native layouts remain unmanaged.

With an existing compatible [b]YANML[/b] setup, Redux can install, update, or remove supported reviewed plugins. YANML itself, including its watcher, injector, and autostart, still needs separate setup.

Native DLLs execute inside the game. Use trusted sources: layout recognition is not a publisher signature, malware scan, or compatibility guarantee.


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/09-themes-and-personalization.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

[b]Set up a workspace that feels comfortable to use.[/b]

Choose English, French, Spanish, Russian, or Simplified Chinese in [b]Preferences > General > Interface language[/b] or Welcome Setup. Missing translations fall back to English; mod names, user content, and date/number formatting remain unchanged. Translation corrections are welcome.

Choose [b]Redux Dark[/b], [b]Redux Light[/b], or [b]Parchment[/b], or edit a custom theme with live previews. Adjust fonts, text size, gradients, category icons, blur, background dimming, and Reduce Motion.

Configure keyboard shortcuts, use keyboard and screen-reader support, or open [b]Quick Access (Ctrl + Q)[/b] to find commands, mods, profiles, orders, themes, and folders.

Welcome Setup introduces the main workflow and can create starter sections for your library.


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/12-privacy.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

Redux runs locally, with [b]no Redux account, advertising, analytics, or general-purpose telemetry[/b]. Core package discovery, load-order editing, diagnostics, saved orders, and save browsing work offline.

Optional provider information, downloads, and application updates use their relevant online services. Your mod list, saves, categories, notes, settings, and diagnostics are not uploaded to a Redux service.

[url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/blob/main/docs/PRIVACY_AND_DATA.md][b]Privacy, local storage & network details[/b][/url]


[center]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/main/docs/assets/nexus-description/13-bugs-feedback-and-support.png?v=3275e4e[/img]
[/center]

Found a bug, have an idea, or need help with a setup?

[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/issues][b]GitHub Issues[/b][/url] — reproducible bugs and focused feature requests. Include your Redux and Windows versions, relevant BG3 patch, steps to reproduce, and what you expected to happen.[/*]
[*][url=https://discord.gg/rJJF89vqFZ][b]Redux Discord[/b][/url] — troubleshooting, discussion, testing feedback, and help narrowing down an issue.[/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/blob/main/docs/FAQ.md][b]FAQ[/b][/url] and [url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/blob/main/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/url] — answers and practical checks.[/*]
[/list]

Developers, mod authors, testers, writers, and designers are welcome to [url=https://github.com/circleainn/BG3ModManager-Redux/blob/main/docs/CONTRIBUTING.md][b]contribute[/b][/url].

[b]Review screenshots and logs before sharing.[/b] Remove personal paths and never post API keys, credentials, signed download links, or private backup archives.


[center]
